&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Shape a brighter financial future with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together with our members, we’re changing the way people think about and interact with personal finance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a next-generation financial services company and national bank using innovative, mobile-first technology to help our millions of members reach their goals. The industry is going through an unprecedented transformation, and we’re at the forefront. We’re proud to come to work every day knowing that what we do has a direct impact on people’s lives, with our core values guiding us every step of the way. &lt;strong&gt;Join us to invest in yourself, your career, and the financial world.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly organized and experienced litigation manager (para-legal) to oversee management of a growing litigation caseload of defaulted loans across 3 national litigation networks and over a hundred local attorney offices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This individual will provide oversight of our active SoFi litigation placements with our attorney network across Personal Loans, Student Loans and Credit Card accounts. They will review each network’s caseload and work on optimizing execution, including assistance with preparations for hearings, mediations, arbitrations, and trials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The role will be responsible for reviewing individual cases, assessing the proposed pleadings, settlement arrangements, and ensuring proper documentation is available and provided as the case demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;They will act as cross-functional liaison between our external litigation network, and SoFi’s in-house counsel, in legal matters that straddle both sides (like a customer’s motion to compel arbitration), and will be expected to have regular engagements with internal partners including, Compliance, Finance, Internal Audit, and Third Party Risk Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;They will work with our Recovery analyst to track performance at the network, state, and product level, introducing key industry metrics/KPIs and delivering regular portfolio reporting to management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;They will evaluate our current litigation engagement model with an eye to improving our internal processes and platforms, identifying workflow gaps and implementing operational enhancements to further our efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;They will demonstrate excellent organizational and project management skills, including the ability to manage multiple complex litigation matters simultaneously while adapting to changing priorities and deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years minimum litigation paralegal experience, preferably managing a caseload of defaulted consumer loans at a FinTech or large bank, or at a law firm or in-house legal department.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree with ABA paralegal certification or Associates/Bachelor’s degree in paralegal studies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience on a litigation case management platform similar to Legal Tracker, CounselLink, or a relational database used to manage litigation caseload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical capabilities and problem-solving skills.&amp;nbsp; Stellar written and verbal communication, and a keen attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
