&lt;li&gt;6+ years as an HR Business Partner with specific HR knowledge in organizational design and development; compensation; performance management; employee engagement;&amp;nbsp; employment law; employee relations; diversity and inclusion; training &amp;amp; employee development; immigration; systems and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS degree in HR, Business, or a related field; or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success influencing and leading at all levels of a corporate hierarchy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in building rapport and tailoring communication to diverse audiences while navigating sensitive situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sharp business acumen with the ability to identify risks and opportunities to drive successful results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in utilizing AI tools to enhance productivity and HR deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience as a leadership coach, driving accountability and aligning stakeholders with competing interests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior problem-solving skills with a focus on creating scalable organizational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional agility, resilience, and the ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high level of accountability and a consistent track record of delivering measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
